# Market-price snapshot — derived external data written by the dashboard's
# prices layer (lib/dashboard/prices.ts), not vault content.
/.cache/

# Rendered CVs — derived artifacts written by `npm run cv:pdf` from the cv.md
# beside them. Binary blobs bloat the vault's audit trail, and the markdown is
# the version worth diffing; the PDF is one command away whenever it's needed.
/jobs/*/cv.pdf

# Progress and form photos — the most sensitive data in the vault, and git
# history is effectively permanent: a body photo committed once stays in the
# repository forever, even after the file is deleted. So they never enter it.
# The other half of the wall is a permission deny rule in
# .claude/settings.json, which stops any agent from reading them at all; the
# user attaches one in conversation on the rare occasion they want feedback.
# The contents are ignored rather than the folder itself, so the folder still
# ships (and stays visible in the vault) with nothing in it but the placeholder.
/fitness/photos/*
!/fitness/photos/.gitkeep

# Obsidian's per-session workspace state (open panes, last cursor position,
# installed community plugin binaries) — noisy and machine-specific, unlike
# the meaningful settings in app.json/core-plugins.json which stay tracked.
/.obsidian/workspace.json
/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
/.obsidian/plugins/
/.obsidian/cache
